{"kind":"assert","text":"Live incident, 2026-08-07: superseding the unratified declared-kinds v1 proposal made the active re-review request project stale, because staleness propagated from the retired draft through the review promise and report that rested on it and into the v2 chain that cites the review findings. Resolved by superseding the supersession, restoring the draft. The structural point: rests_on carries two different relations — a governing basis, whose death should flare dependents, and historical lineage, whose retirement should not — and the fold treats them alike. This is a new facet of the open projection-honesty request, and the declared-kinds design's basis constraints are the natural place to give the two relations distinct names. Until then the working discipline is: never retire an unratified draft that later acts rest on; let ratification select among live proposals."}